1
00:00:00,096 --> 00:00:01,361
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,363 --> 00:00:02,929
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:02,931 --> 00:00:04,082
(Episode 15)

4
00:00:04,085 --> 00:00:05,209
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

5
00:00:08,148 --> 00:00:09,506
I'm sorry.

6
00:00:10,819 --> 00:00:13,130
It's acute pediatric blood cancer.

7
00:00:19,427 --> 00:00:20,511
Mai.

8
00:00:21,083 --> 00:00:23,241
Then...

9
00:00:23,473 --> 00:00:28,003
what should we do about O Reum now?

10
00:00:28,275 --> 00:00:30,461
We'll start chemotherapy.

11
00:00:30,928 --> 00:00:32,054
Then...

12
00:00:32,304 --> 00:00:33,844
will he be okay?

13
00:00:33,902 --> 00:00:35,372
Can he recover?

14
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:38,407
We'll proceed
with intensive chemotherapy...

15
00:00:38,409 --> 00:00:40,865
in multiple stages.

16
00:00:41,001 --> 00:00:43,883
However, there are genetic findings
that indicate a high risk of relapse,

17
00:00:43,908 --> 00:00:46,323
so it's difficult
to guarantee the outcome.

18
00:00:47,181 --> 00:00:50,008
But we will do our best.

19
00:00:55,062 --> 00:00:58,813
The polar bear said
to the children saying goodbye,

20
00:00:58,948 --> 00:01:00,314
"Take care."

21
00:01:00,384 --> 00:01:03,534
"Stay healthy."

22
00:01:06,128 --> 00:01:07,446
Your uncle's good at this, right?

23
00:01:07,503 --> 00:01:08,999
More fun than your dad, right?

24
00:01:09,024 --> 00:01:11,619
You work at a broadcasting station.

25
00:01:11,643 --> 00:01:12,733
That's right.

26
00:01:12,757 --> 00:01:14,654
I'm a director.

27
00:01:14,679 --> 00:01:18,422
- What do you want to be when you grow up?
- A singer.

28
00:01:18,595 --> 00:01:20,730
I want to dance and sing.

29
00:01:20,754 --> 00:01:22,003
And go to clubs.

30
00:01:22,028 --> 00:01:24,344
I want to go to clubs.

31
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:35,259
What did the doctor say?

32
00:01:35,939 --> 00:01:37,356
It's not true, right?

33
00:01:38,626 --> 00:01:40,710
- O Reum.
- Why are you crying?

34
00:02:09,921 --> 00:02:11,269
Are you going to keep doing this?

35
00:02:11,293 --> 00:02:12,615
Stop crying!

36
00:02:30,408 --> 00:02:31,771
Right.

37
00:02:31,784 --> 00:02:32,995
Ji Ni.

38
00:02:33,346 --> 00:02:36,606
This is it.
Let's make a great children's storybook.

39
00:02:36,631 --> 00:02:38,333
Is this something you really wanted to do?

40
00:02:38,357 --> 00:02:39,818
Of course!

41
00:02:39,843 --> 00:02:41,937
People say video is everything now,

42
00:02:42,001 --> 00:02:44,617
but when we were kids,
we still read a lot of storybooks.

43
00:02:44,762 --> 00:02:47,875
- Those simple illustrations...
- Sparked our imagination?

44
00:02:48,035 --> 00:02:50,134
Yes, exactly.

45
00:02:50,188 --> 00:02:52,981
If we leave more room
for children's imaginations,

46
00:02:53,031 --> 00:02:55,331
couldn't Korean animation grow further?

47
00:02:56,488 --> 00:03:01,350
I want to create spaces where children
can fill in parts of the story themselves.

48
00:03:01,375 --> 00:03:02,929
That's a great idea.

49
00:03:02,968 --> 00:03:06,466
There's someone who thinks
exactly like I do.

50
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:09,493
- That's amazing.
- I'm the one who's amazed.

51
00:03:09,908 --> 00:03:12,514
At first, I was going to do it with Ji Hu,

52
00:03:12,673 --> 00:03:14,378
but he's a pianist.

53
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:15,868
Do you know how sensitive he is?

54
00:03:16,184 --> 00:03:17,807
People in music tend to be like that.

55
00:03:17,941 --> 00:03:19,107
My mom is the same.

56
00:03:19,132 --> 00:03:21,540
They obsess over even a semitone.

57
00:03:21,781 --> 00:03:23,392
My dad said it drives him crazy.

58
00:03:23,416 --> 00:03:24,945
That's right.

59
00:03:26,942 --> 00:03:28,603
Feels like you're talking about me.

60
00:03:29,715 --> 00:03:31,377
Hey, when did you get here?

61
00:03:31,815 --> 00:03:33,843
It's rude to talk about someone
behind their back.

62
00:03:36,006 --> 00:03:37,006
Hello.

63
00:03:38,027 --> 00:03:39,531
Hello.

64
00:03:41,854 --> 00:03:45,095
This is far from your original major.
Are you okay with that?

65
00:03:45,477 --> 00:03:46,523
Yes.

66
00:03:46,741 --> 00:03:49,034
I wasn't really into fine art
to begin with.

67
00:03:49,682 --> 00:03:53,075
I only pursued it because my mom wanted it
and my dad liked it,

68
00:03:53,145 --> 00:03:57,582
but it wasn't truly what I wanted to do,
so I felt stifled while doing it.

69
00:03:58,448 --> 00:04:00,303
And you still painted that well?

70
00:04:00,715 --> 00:04:03,155
You must be a genius.

71
00:04:03,328 --> 00:04:05,517
You're quick to jump to conclusions.

72
00:04:06,763 --> 00:04:09,153
I'm truly sorry
about what happened before.

73
00:04:09,629 --> 00:04:11,108
I've reflected on it a lot.

74
00:04:11,282 --> 00:04:14,168
But what I said about your art is sincere.

75
00:04:14,728 --> 00:04:16,390
Your drawings feel...

76
00:04:16,474 --> 00:04:19,097
comforting yet strong,

77
00:04:19,841 --> 00:04:21,315
and very compelling.

78
00:04:22,202 --> 00:04:24,403
If you draw the main characters
with that kind of feeling,

79
00:04:24,428 --> 00:04:27,802
I believe we'll get a children's book
with a completely different atmosphere.

80
00:04:29,097 --> 00:04:30,700
Thank you.

81
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:35,022
Before my dad passed away,
he supported my dream.

82
00:04:35,102 --> 00:04:36,447
He told me I should go for it.

83
00:04:39,548 --> 00:04:41,504
My dad was in the Navy.

84
00:04:41,664 --> 00:04:43,510
After retiring,
he said he would make books,

85
00:04:43,534 --> 00:04:46,166
and I thought it was just a hobby,
but it wasn't.

86
00:04:47,188 --> 00:04:49,567
He said that since young people these days
don't read much,

87
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:52,314
we should help them get closer
to books again.

88
00:04:55,398 --> 00:04:56,758
Please help Tae O with this.

89
00:04:56,783 --> 00:04:58,278
I still have a lot to learn.

90
00:04:58,322 --> 00:04:59,771
I'll trust you and follow your lead.

91
00:04:59,822 --> 00:05:01,695
I'll do my best too.

92
00:05:03,822 --> 00:05:05,621
That's the first time I've seen you smile.

93
00:05:06,495 --> 00:05:08,309
So you can smile like that too?

94
00:05:10,254 --> 00:05:11,254
Yes.

95
00:05:11,432 --> 00:05:13,062
It depends on the person.

96
00:05:15,142 --> 00:05:16,210
I'm sorry.

97
00:05:16,235 --> 00:05:17,684
I had you all wrong.

98
00:05:21,858 --> 00:05:23,849
Please don't say things like that anymore.

99
00:05:23,879 --> 00:05:25,342
It makes me uncomfortable.

100
00:05:26,838 --> 00:05:27,838
Okay.

101
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:32,208
How is your injury now?

102
00:05:34,231 --> 00:05:35,496
I'm fine.

103
00:05:36,488 --> 00:05:37,995
I'm serious.

104
00:05:38,152 --> 00:05:39,668
Please be careful.

105
00:05:40,918 --> 00:05:41,918
Okay.

106
00:05:43,862 --> 00:05:45,007
Right.

107
00:05:45,038 --> 00:05:47,619
I saw your account.

108
00:05:48,308 --> 00:05:49,823
So I told Ji Hu about it.

109
00:05:49,849 --> 00:05:51,757
Why would you tell him that?

110
00:05:51,782 --> 00:05:53,428
Do you know how hard
that made things for me?

111
00:05:53,453 --> 00:05:55,903
But that was your fault, Do Hee.

112
00:05:55,905 --> 00:05:57,418
What did I do wrong?

113
00:05:57,611 --> 00:06:00,427
It was just for fun,
how could you go running to tell him?

114
00:06:00,623 --> 00:06:02,698
I can't listen to this nonsense.

115
00:06:03,302 --> 00:06:06,835
You get caught stealing
and then complain about getting caught?

116
00:06:07,322 --> 00:06:08,557
Hey, be quiet.

117
00:06:08,582 --> 00:06:10,787
This isn't the time for you to argue.

118
00:06:10,834 --> 00:06:12,744
Do you think that's the only thing
you've been caught for?

119
00:06:12,834 --> 00:06:14,977
- What else?
- If you keep it up, you'll get caught.

120
00:06:15,002 --> 00:06:16,401
There are no secrets in this world.

121
00:06:16,442 --> 00:06:17,955
The truth always comes out.

122
00:06:17,980 --> 00:06:19,142
Jeon Jung A.

123
00:06:20,929 --> 00:06:22,469
Anyway, I'm sorry...

124
00:06:22,494 --> 00:06:25,370
if I caused trouble between you and Ji Hu.

125
00:06:27,368 --> 00:06:31,326
Still, Ji Hu must be angry
because he loves you.

126
00:06:37,015 --> 00:06:40,853
Why are you two coming
in together this morning?

127
00:06:44,395 --> 00:06:46,553
She's acting weird again.

128
00:06:48,615 --> 00:06:50,181
Why are you like this?
I said we'd talk later.

129
00:06:50,206 --> 00:06:52,207
How am I supposed to live like this
when I'm so frustrated?

130
00:06:52,611 --> 00:06:54,978
What business do you have meeting
Na Ji Ni this early?

131
00:06:55,003 --> 00:06:56,563
Are you the one cheating?

132
00:06:57,755 --> 00:07:00,049
You pretend to care about me
while secretly seeing Na Ji Ni?

133
00:07:00,074 --> 00:07:02,563
- Do Do Hee...
- Then explain it quickly!

134
00:07:05,368 --> 00:07:07,349
I found out Ji Ni wasn't the school bully.

135
00:07:07,374 --> 00:07:08,374
What?

136
00:07:09,455 --> 00:07:12,108
Who told you that? Na Ji Ni, right?

137
00:07:12,518 --> 00:07:13,924
Why did you lie?

138
00:07:14,995 --> 00:07:17,578
- It's not a lie.
- Why did you lie?

139
00:07:19,708 --> 00:07:22,406
If I tell you, will you forgive me?

140
00:07:22,756 --> 00:07:24,101
If you tell me honestly.

141
00:07:27,145 --> 00:07:29,543
At first, it was a joke,

142
00:07:30,638 --> 00:07:32,430
but things kept getting bigger.

143
00:07:34,274 --> 00:07:36,291
I was scared
and was going to tell the truth,

144
00:07:36,315 --> 00:07:38,804
but then dad had his election.

145
00:07:39,842 --> 00:07:41,462
Mom told me not to say anything.

146
00:07:41,487 --> 00:07:43,055
Then why did you say you were the one
who got hit?

147
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:45,402
Because in my heart,
I was the one who got hurt!

148
00:07:45,505 --> 00:07:47,025
Ji Ni was completely fine.

149
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:49,057
Would a completely fine person
drop out of high school?

150
00:07:49,101 --> 00:07:51,308
That's why I ran away to England too.

151
00:07:51,602 --> 00:07:53,304
Because I hated everything.

152
00:07:54,802 --> 00:07:56,718
Then I met you,

153
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:59,219
and I wanted to tell you how I felt.

154
00:08:01,499 --> 00:08:02,812
Don't you get it?

155
00:08:03,374 --> 00:08:05,389
Do the visible facts really matter?

156
00:08:05,462 --> 00:08:08,007
- What matters is how I feel.
- Because of you,

157
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:12,240
I judged based only on what I saw,
and I seriously wronged Ji Ni.

158
00:08:16,988 --> 00:08:18,233
The staff will be here soon.

159
00:08:18,257 --> 00:08:19,387
Let's talk tonight.

160
00:08:19,462 --> 00:08:21,370
You won't get mad, right?

161
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,405
We'll talk later.

162
00:08:25,908 --> 00:08:27,187
Do Hee!

163
00:08:29,188 --> 00:08:31,417
Are you really that fed up with me?

164
00:08:32,162 --> 00:08:34,116
This is so humiliating.

165
00:08:34,202 --> 00:08:36,076
I hate this kind of vague,
half-baked situation!

166
00:08:36,101 --> 00:08:37,509
Do you still not get it?

167
00:08:38,208 --> 00:08:40,166
I won't do it again.

168
00:08:41,034 --> 00:08:42,470
I'll be more careful.

169
00:08:43,822 --> 00:08:45,164
Give me a hug.

170
00:08:47,801 --> 00:08:49,083
Please, Ji Hu.

171
00:08:49,807 --> 00:08:52,359
If my mom finds out you caught me,

172
00:08:53,482 --> 00:08:54,809
I'm done for.

173
00:08:55,788 --> 00:08:56,788
Okay?

174
00:09:00,955 --> 00:09:03,064
What if we expand investment
in Indonesia even more?

175
00:09:03,095 --> 00:09:05,025
- More than this?
- You said it's a good opportunity.

176
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:07,294
Still, you should prepare
for the unexpected.

177
00:09:07,364 --> 00:09:08,718
Going all-in is risky.

178
00:09:16,654 --> 00:09:19,124
Why aren't you coming?
You promised you would.

179
00:09:19,149 --> 00:09:20,819
Right now is a bit...

180
00:09:22,672 --> 00:09:24,206
It's hard for me to go.

181
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,078
- Later.
- When is later?

182
00:09:26,115 --> 00:09:27,829
Do you really want me to do as I please?

183
00:09:28,631 --> 00:09:29,674
If you don't want to work,

184
00:09:29,676 --> 00:09:32,583
just sign the share waiver and send it.
Why are you dragging this out?

185
00:09:32,847 --> 00:09:35,067
You can't go back
to the broadcasting station.

186
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:37,742
If you get entangled in an affair,
you're finished in this country.

187
00:09:37,828 --> 00:09:39,084
Haven't you seen it happen?

188
00:09:40,196 --> 00:09:41,196
Hang up.

189
00:09:42,842 --> 00:09:44,108
So stupid.

190
00:09:47,366 --> 00:09:48,783
I'll invest more.

191
00:09:48,807 --> 00:09:49,896
I've made my decision.

192
00:09:49,921 --> 00:09:54,301
And I heard all the dramas
in preparation were halted.

193
00:09:54,367 --> 00:09:56,467
Can we restart those too?

194
00:09:56,751 --> 00:09:57,803
I'll take charge.

195
00:09:57,828 --> 00:10:00,759
I'll step in as CEO myself.

196
00:10:00,783 --> 00:10:02,086
Are you going to do it yourself?

197
00:10:02,219 --> 00:10:03,359
Yes.

198
00:10:03,429 --> 00:10:05,129
Why? Do you think I can't do it?

199
00:10:05,701 --> 00:10:07,462
I'll learn as I go.

200
00:10:18,975 --> 00:10:21,320
- Hey!
- Let go!

201
00:10:21,322 --> 00:10:22,506
Come out with me!

202
00:10:22,808 --> 00:10:24,976
What are you doing? Let go!

203
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:33,780
You daughter of a homewrecker.

204
00:10:33,828 --> 00:10:36,842
- Stay away from Ji Hu.
- What?

205
00:10:37,036 --> 00:10:38,881
Like mother, like daughter.

206
00:10:46,348 --> 00:10:48,919
What are you staring at? You little...

207
00:10:54,261 --> 00:10:56,050
I told you I wouldn't just take it again.

208
00:11:00,182 --> 00:11:02,245
Why is someone as filthy
as you seeing Ji Hu?

209
00:11:02,247 --> 00:11:04,235
Are you scared? Worried I might steal him?

210
00:11:05,468 --> 00:11:07,870
Ji Hu has high standards.

211
00:11:07,872 --> 00:11:09,841
You think he'd even look
at someone like you?

212
00:11:09,902 --> 00:11:12,257
And do you know how amazing his mom is?

213
00:11:12,259 --> 00:11:15,361
- Your mom wouldn't even stand a chance.
- Then I'll test...

214
00:11:15,788 --> 00:11:19,214
- just how high his standards are.
- You little...

215
00:11:21,181 --> 00:11:23,135
Stop it. This is a workplace.

216
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:28,046
Leave. And don't ever come back.

217
00:11:28,088 --> 00:11:29,519
Your face makes me sick.

218
00:11:32,339 --> 00:11:33,663
You crazy bitch!

219
00:11:58,534 --> 00:11:59,855
Is that you, O Reum?

220
00:12:02,291 --> 00:12:03,894
I've seen you before.

221
00:12:05,027 --> 00:12:09,268
- Are you sick?
- Yeah, I got a shot this big.

222
00:12:09,715 --> 00:12:12,988
I didn't cry. My mom did.

223
00:12:13,014 --> 00:12:16,346
Really? You're so brave.

224
00:12:17,232 --> 00:12:19,045
Where did it hurt so much?

225
00:12:19,248 --> 00:12:20,727
Looks like you're here for treatment.

226
00:12:21,268 --> 00:12:22,548
That injury is taking a while to heal.

227
00:12:23,837 --> 00:12:25,735
It's almost healed.

228
00:12:26,785 --> 00:12:27,882
That's a relief.

229
00:12:32,128 --> 00:12:33,939
Is O Reum sick?

230
00:12:35,415 --> 00:12:36,925
Yeah, a little.

231
00:12:40,888 --> 00:12:42,802
- Let's go.
- Bye.

232
00:12:52,231 --> 00:12:54,681
(Pediatric and Adolescent Cancer Center)

233
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:13,694
- Who was that?
- The drawing lady.

234
00:13:13,732 --> 00:13:15,119
"The drawing lady?"

235
00:13:17,041 --> 00:13:20,775
He saw her on the way here.

236
00:13:21,488 --> 00:13:24,928
- I guess they got close at the funeral.
- At the funeral?

237
00:13:27,762 --> 00:13:30,358
- Why is she here?
- I guess the injury she got...

238
00:13:30,704 --> 00:13:32,029
because of me still hasn't healed.

239
00:13:33,317 --> 00:13:34,535
She turns up everywhere.

240
00:13:35,675 --> 00:13:36,679
O Reum,

241
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:39,660
- do you like her?
- Yeah, she's nice.

242
00:13:39,662 --> 00:13:40,761
Is she nice?

243
00:13:41,108 --> 00:13:42,667
How do you know she's nice?

244
00:13:48,562 --> 00:13:52,841
Then she knew O Reum was sick?

245
00:13:53,303 --> 00:13:55,817
No. I didn't tell her.

246
00:13:56,602 --> 00:13:59,228
I felt bad that she was still hurt.

247
00:14:15,121 --> 00:14:17,976
(Pediatric and Adolescent Cancer Center)

248
00:14:18,643 --> 00:14:20,121
No way...

249
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,781
Yes.

250
00:14:41,783 --> 00:14:42,814
Mom.

251
00:14:43,801 --> 00:14:46,312
- You're here.
- Are you working?

252
00:14:47,008 --> 00:14:48,640
Does it look like I'm playing around?

253
00:14:49,549 --> 00:14:51,723
You even know how to use Excel?

254
00:14:53,231 --> 00:14:55,410
I just learned it. I'm still practicing.

255
00:14:56,645 --> 00:14:58,523
Ji Ni, I'm...

256
00:14:58,644 --> 00:15:00,589
going to run your dad's company.

257
00:15:00,591 --> 00:15:01,739
You are?

258
00:15:01,748 --> 00:15:03,173
Why are you so surprised?

259
00:15:03,175 --> 00:15:06,165
Did you think I'd starve
if I couldn't play the cello?

260
00:15:06,168 --> 00:15:08,988
I thought you were hiring
a professional manager.

261
00:15:09,048 --> 00:15:11,580
Maybe I will,
but I should know what's going on first.

262
00:15:11,582 --> 00:15:13,202
I've spent my whole life
reading sheet music.

263
00:15:14,404 --> 00:15:16,267
I figured I should learn the basics.

264
00:15:16,651 --> 00:15:18,089
It's actually kind of fun.

265
00:15:19,902 --> 00:15:20,948
Look.

266
00:15:22,629 --> 00:15:24,648
- Is this dad's computer?
- Yeah.

267
00:15:28,648 --> 00:15:29,669
- What?
- What?

268
00:15:30,050 --> 00:15:31,731
What's this doing here?

269
00:15:31,822 --> 00:15:34,541
Remember this? This is Morocco.

270
00:15:35,328 --> 00:15:37,812
How would I remember? I was so little.

271
00:15:43,452 --> 00:15:45,624
They're all pictures of you, Mom.

272
00:15:45,626 --> 00:15:49,424
Of course. Your dad only had eyes for me.

273
00:15:49,565 --> 00:15:53,228
- What about you?
- What do you mean?

274
00:15:53,882 --> 00:15:55,438
We were...

275
00:15:55,890 --> 00:15:58,639
each other's news, inspiration,

276
00:15:58,641 --> 00:16:00,222
and we admired each other.

277
00:16:01,046 --> 00:16:03,528
"Admired." I like that word.

278
00:16:05,729 --> 00:16:07,055
Hold on.

279
00:16:08,502 --> 00:16:09,860
Yes, Counselor.

280
00:16:10,801 --> 00:16:11,815
Yes.

281
00:16:12,951 --> 00:16:15,933
(CEO Cha Min Ki)

282
00:16:15,935 --> 00:16:17,419
Dad.

283
00:16:21,347 --> 00:16:22,640
I see.

284
00:16:23,637 --> 00:16:24,662
Yes.

285
00:16:32,949 --> 00:16:34,194
Dad.

286
00:16:49,475 --> 00:16:52,248
Excuse me, he injured his leg.
He has a prosthetic leg.

287
00:17:03,181 --> 00:17:06,095
Ji Ni, why are you crying?

288
00:17:09,401 --> 00:17:11,862
I miss my dad, Mom.

289
00:17:27,902 --> 00:17:29,395
Please clear one place setting.

290
00:17:29,397 --> 00:17:31,076
Isn't the director coming?

291
00:17:31,078 --> 00:17:33,442
Just leave it. What's the harm?

292
00:17:33,862 --> 00:17:36,558
He passed away. Clear it away.

293
00:17:38,212 --> 00:17:39,639
Yes, I'm sorry.

294
00:17:46,041 --> 00:17:47,968
Why can't we just leave it?

295
00:17:48,122 --> 00:17:50,228
It feels like my dad might still come.

296
00:17:50,902 --> 00:17:54,235
How can you say he's gone so easily?

297
00:17:54,328 --> 00:17:56,150
He's gone. That's the reality.

298
00:17:56,281 --> 00:17:58,017
It's just you and me now.

299
00:17:58,042 --> 00:17:59,655
Stop fooling yourself and let go.

300
00:17:59,795 --> 00:18:02,108
- I'm not like you.
- Right.

301
00:18:02,347 --> 00:18:05,167
You told Dr. Hwang you keep thinking...

302
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:06,720
he's at home or just at work.

303
00:18:06,722 --> 00:18:09,235
I wanted to say something then,
but I held back. Don't do that.

304
00:18:10,115 --> 00:18:12,727
Then why did you hold two funerals,

305
00:18:12,729 --> 00:18:15,342
- and even get into a fight over it?
- Because that's where I drew the line.

306
00:18:19,275 --> 00:18:21,095
Look how my lessons are disappearing.

307
00:18:23,012 --> 00:18:24,992
See how fickle the world is?

308
00:18:26,301 --> 00:18:29,064
Getting kicked out of the orchestra
was probably the biggest reason.

309
00:18:29,942 --> 00:18:32,444
Did your other students quit too?

310
00:18:34,219 --> 00:18:36,339
Why? Do you feel sorry for me?

311
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:38,502
No.

312
00:18:38,855 --> 00:18:40,742
It's the price you had to pay.

313
00:18:41,082 --> 00:18:42,101
But...

314
00:18:43,122 --> 00:18:45,041
it's dragging on longer than I expected.

315
00:18:46,328 --> 00:18:48,115
Yeah, it is.

316
00:18:49,382 --> 00:18:51,435
People never let things go.

317
00:18:52,875 --> 00:18:56,635
If I were diagnosed
with a terminal illness like your dad,

318
00:18:58,562 --> 00:19:01,148
I'd kill them, then die in prison.

319
00:19:02,008 --> 00:19:04,688
Dying in a hospital or prison
makes no difference to me.

320
00:19:04,706 --> 00:19:06,542
- Mom.
- No Yeong Ju...

321
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,955
I hated her more than you can imagine.

322
00:19:11,189 --> 00:19:13,067
Talk about nerve.

323
00:19:14,408 --> 00:19:16,968
No one likes having their love
interfered with.

324
00:19:17,108 --> 00:19:20,161
So it's okay for her to hate me,
but not okay for me to hate her?

325
00:19:20,163 --> 00:19:21,632
I'm a woman too.

326
00:19:23,566 --> 00:19:26,442
Yeah, I should've just let it go.

327
00:19:27,482 --> 00:19:29,160
That's what your grandmother said too.

328
00:19:29,162 --> 00:19:31,067
She told me to just look the other way.

329
00:19:31,203 --> 00:19:33,946
To move on after losing the baby.

330
00:19:34,375 --> 00:19:37,637
Go back to Europe
and keep performing there.

331
00:19:37,816 --> 00:19:39,192
Why didn't you?

332
00:19:40,849 --> 00:19:42,228
Are you stupid?

333
00:19:42,588 --> 00:19:45,862
If I could let go that easily,
would I have loved him at all?

334
00:19:46,408 --> 00:19:49,281
Did you really love him that much?

335
00:19:49,492 --> 00:19:53,035
He wasn't rich or even that handsome.

336
00:19:55,295 --> 00:19:58,606
That's why your grandmother
beat her chest in frustration.

337
00:19:58,608 --> 00:20:01,971
There were plenty of rich men
and plenty of handsome ones.

338
00:20:03,399 --> 00:20:04,948
I just...

339
00:20:06,637 --> 00:20:07,708
fell in love.

340
00:20:09,971 --> 00:20:12,444
I couldn't even perform without your dad.

341
00:20:12,846 --> 00:20:15,218
I could only play when he was watching.

342
00:20:15,221 --> 00:20:17,334
I wanted to earn your dad's approval.

343
00:20:18,249 --> 00:20:19,600
Other critics...

344
00:20:20,124 --> 00:20:21,615
didn't matter.

345
00:20:22,805 --> 00:20:24,560
That's how we were.

346
00:20:25,513 --> 00:20:29,131
Your dad worked himself to the bone...

347
00:20:29,977 --> 00:20:31,398
to create something that would move me.

348
00:20:32,721 --> 00:20:34,382
His office was proof of that.

349
00:20:47,930 --> 00:20:51,506
This is my final farewell to the director.

350
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,840
Please accept it.

351
00:20:56,227 --> 00:20:58,144
Thank you. I will.

352
00:21:14,507 --> 00:21:16,949
- The cancer center?
- Yeah.

353
00:21:17,221 --> 00:21:18,983
That's where he was headed.

354
00:21:19,430 --> 00:21:20,949
I'm sure it's nothing serious.

355
00:21:23,930 --> 00:21:25,582
You're about to say something awful
again, right?

356
00:21:25,721 --> 00:21:28,101
- Don't.
- No, I'm going to.

357
00:21:28,555 --> 00:21:29,815
Did you forget?

358
00:21:30,208 --> 00:21:32,053
His mom came all the way here...

359
00:21:32,055 --> 00:21:33,486
trying to take this house.

360
00:21:33,555 --> 00:21:35,522
She claims
she's the daughter of a Vietnamese tycoon.

361
00:21:35,596 --> 00:21:37,230
Does she have no shame?

362
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,430
No wonder her son turned out that way.

363
00:21:39,471 --> 00:21:42,464
Mom, what did he ever do wrong?

364
00:21:42,596 --> 00:21:43,928
Whether she was greedy or not,

365
00:21:43,930 --> 00:21:45,562
her son is innocent.

366
00:21:45,948 --> 00:21:47,846
How can you say that while looking at me?

367
00:21:47,888 --> 00:21:49,055
Fine.

368
00:21:50,263 --> 00:21:51,921
You say everything you want,
then just say "fine."

369
00:21:52,508 --> 00:21:54,469
O Reum did nothing wrong,
so don't ever say that again.

370
00:21:54,471 --> 00:21:56,096
Fine. Enough.

371
00:22:00,846 --> 00:22:02,013
That girl!

372
00:22:05,513 --> 00:22:07,935
By the way, is he really sick?

373
00:22:10,062 --> 00:22:12,110
Yeong Ju's been dealt a terrible blow.

374
00:22:28,639 --> 00:22:31,678
- Mom.
- Eat here before you go.

375
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:33,053
I can go and eat with them.

376
00:22:33,055 --> 00:22:34,781
O Reum wants to eat it.

377
00:22:34,888 --> 00:22:37,013
You have to take turns so he won't notice.

378
00:22:38,305 --> 00:22:40,805
Let's talk sitting down.

379
00:22:40,846 --> 00:22:42,119
My neck hurts.

380
00:22:42,388 --> 00:22:44,539
You always stand there
until I tell you to sit.

381
00:22:46,930 --> 00:22:47,930
Yes.

382
00:22:51,680 --> 00:22:53,516
It's the gimbap Mai likes.

383
00:22:53,555 --> 00:22:55,363
She looks so worn out these past few days.

384
00:22:55,930 --> 00:22:58,055
- Take good care of her.
- Yes.

385
00:22:59,638 --> 00:23:01,658
I heard he's still getting IVs.

386
00:23:02,388 --> 00:23:04,399
When he throws up,
you take care of everything.

387
00:23:04,650 --> 00:23:08,079
And tell Mai not to cry
in front of O Reum.

388
00:23:08,471 --> 00:23:10,774
- Okay.
- What about work?

389
00:23:11,013 --> 00:23:12,388
I took a few days off.

390
00:23:12,805 --> 00:23:13,971
Good.

391
00:23:15,638 --> 00:23:16,918
I hope...

392
00:23:17,253 --> 00:23:18,975
the IV works well for him.

393
00:23:23,333 --> 00:23:24,917
- Already?
- I can't eat more.

394
00:23:24,930 --> 00:23:26,364
- I'll be off.
- Okay.

395
00:23:29,888 --> 00:23:31,053
Take care.

396
00:23:31,055 --> 00:23:32,055
Okay.

397
00:23:40,346 --> 00:23:41,388
Hello.

398
00:23:41,397 --> 00:23:43,605
- Hello.
- Hello.

399
00:23:44,263 --> 00:23:46,428
What's all this?

400
00:23:46,430 --> 00:23:48,385
I heard O Reum is sick.

401
00:23:48,388 --> 00:23:50,510
It's meshima mushroom and green juice.

402
00:23:50,513 --> 00:23:52,317
He can't have things like this.

403
00:23:52,680 --> 00:23:54,055
Thank you, but what should I do?

404
00:23:54,096 --> 00:23:56,136
Then at least have the family eat it.

405
00:23:56,138 --> 00:23:57,712
I can have the green juice,

406
00:23:58,930 --> 00:24:00,598
but meshima mushroom is expensive.

407
00:24:01,430 --> 00:24:02,969
Who gave this?

408
00:24:02,971 --> 00:24:04,346
I'll return it.

409
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:05,888
Thank you.

410
00:24:06,971 --> 00:24:08,260
Stay strong.

411
00:24:08,281 --> 00:24:09,396
I will.

412
00:24:10,180 --> 00:24:12,868
Thinking about such a young child
having to endure this,

413
00:24:13,570 --> 00:24:15,379
it breaks my heart.

414
00:24:17,240 --> 00:24:19,818
How about we do a more upbeat song?

415
00:24:20,342 --> 00:24:21,611
Let's sing "Die Forelle."

416
00:24:21,971 --> 00:24:23,081
Sounds good.

417
00:24:39,971 --> 00:24:41,788
- I'll get going.
- Okay.

418
00:24:47,971 --> 00:24:49,180
Sa Bin.

419
00:24:51,388 --> 00:24:53,261
I was making gimbap for my son
and daughter-in-law at the hospital,

420
00:24:53,263 --> 00:24:54,638
so I made an extra roll.

421
00:24:54,999 --> 00:24:56,666
I can't promise it'll taste great.

422
00:24:57,430 --> 00:25:00,044
My daughter-in-law likes cilantro,

423
00:25:00,047 --> 00:25:01,428
so I added some. I hope you like it.

424
00:25:01,430 --> 00:25:03,102
I like cilantro too.

425
00:25:03,471 --> 00:25:04,638
That's a relief.

426
00:25:04,647 --> 00:25:08,288
Thanks for driving me home that day.

427
00:25:08,555 --> 00:25:11,261
And when did you put
a hangover remedy in my bag?

428
00:25:11,263 --> 00:25:12,868
That's just basic courtesy.

429
00:25:13,638 --> 00:25:14,918
But Mrs. No,

430
00:25:15,236 --> 00:25:18,349
- do you play favorites too?
- Me?

431
00:25:18,388 --> 00:25:20,846
You seemed pretty hard on your second son.

432
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,513
That kid is just...

433
00:25:23,555 --> 00:25:25,675
It's not favoritism.

434
00:25:25,763 --> 00:25:29,592
He's the troublemaker of the family,
so I did scold him a lot.

435
00:25:29,680 --> 00:25:31,584
I was a difficult teenager too.

436
00:25:31,711 --> 00:25:33,013
Were you?

437
00:25:33,055 --> 00:25:35,055
I thought you were a model child.

438
00:25:35,096 --> 00:25:36,305
No.

439
00:25:36,805 --> 00:25:39,721
After my mom gave birth to me,
she became very ill and passed away.

440
00:25:39,888 --> 00:25:43,110
I carried a lot of guilt,
thinking my mom was unhappy because of me.

441
00:25:44,151 --> 00:25:46,465
I heard you became a widow...

442
00:25:46,475 --> 00:25:48,469
not long after having your second son.

443
00:25:48,471 --> 00:25:50,305
Did I tell you that too?

444
00:25:51,515 --> 00:25:53,839
I guess I really was drunk that day.

445
00:25:55,375 --> 00:25:58,247
Please show your second son
a little more love.

446
00:25:58,257 --> 00:26:00,678
When I saw him that day,
he reminded me of myself.

447
00:26:00,680 --> 00:26:02,305
It really broke my heart.

448
00:26:03,305 --> 00:26:05,147
I've never thought about it that way,

449
00:26:05,305 --> 00:26:06,555
but I'll keep that in mind.

450
00:26:06,596 --> 00:26:07,805
Thank you.

451
00:26:08,888 --> 00:26:11,198
I'll enjoy this thoughtful lunch.

452
00:26:13,846 --> 00:26:15,247
And...

453
00:26:15,388 --> 00:26:18,930
I'll be rooting for O Reum
to get through his treatment.

454
00:26:19,628 --> 00:26:21,792
- You got this.
- Thank you.

455
00:26:23,930 --> 00:26:25,513
Give it to me.

456
00:26:28,028 --> 00:26:30,053
Did you buy all these books?

457
00:26:30,055 --> 00:26:31,469
They're all good books.

458
00:26:31,471 --> 00:26:33,638
I had no idea there were so many
great books in the world.

459
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:35,680
They're so interesting. I love them.

460
00:26:36,013 --> 00:26:37,219
Take them to the car and come back.

461
00:26:37,221 --> 00:26:38,563
I'm going to look around more.

462
00:26:38,721 --> 00:26:39,721
More?

463
00:26:41,305 --> 00:26:42,513
Again...

464
00:26:47,805 --> 00:26:51,888
(Turtle Bus,
Audio Storybook Listening Booth)

465
00:27:11,305 --> 00:27:13,098
Do you need some help?

466
00:27:13,346 --> 00:27:14,721
Yes.

467
00:27:47,474 --> 00:27:49,471
You can turn it on here.

468
00:27:49,555 --> 00:27:51,471
There it is. Thank you.

469
00:28:16,221 --> 00:28:19,471
(Family Register)

470
00:28:19,513 --> 00:28:22,385
I guess he's really planning
to expand the publishing company.

471
00:28:22,388 --> 00:28:24,930
The girl I met today
is also very interested in fairy tales.

472
00:28:25,013 --> 00:28:27,719
It really bothers me.

473
00:28:27,721 --> 00:28:30,096
Because I want to see O Reum.

474
00:28:30,138 --> 00:28:32,388
I heard O Reum is sick.
Is it really cancer?

475
00:28:32,430 --> 00:28:34,221
At this rate,
there'll be one funeral after another.

476
00:28:34,263 --> 00:28:36,511
You have so many fans,

477
00:28:36,513 --> 00:28:38,096
so why did you get close to me?

478
00:28:38,099 --> 00:28:39,126
Want to know?

479
00:28:39,129 --> 00:28:41,886
I was just drunk
and went there in the middle of the night.

480
00:28:42,642 --> 00:28:44,642
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
